==English==

===Etymology===
{{onom|en}}. Connected with {{m|en|splash}} and {{m|en|splish}}; compare also {{m|en|slosh}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/splɑʃ/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/splɒʃ/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-splosh.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒʃ|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To splash with a heavy [[splash]]ing sound.
#: {{ux|en|'''splosh''' into the sea}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Conversation with the Mann| author=John Ridley| year=2009| text=Sometimes someone would take a wrench to a fire hydrant, jam a crate up to its nozzle, turning the whole of it into a fountain for us kids to '''splosh''' around and play in.}}
# To [[traverse]] [[mushy]] or [[marshy]] wetlands.
# To [[spill]] or [[spill over]].

